  "assumptions": [
    "Neutral opaque seeds isolate endpoint and placement behavior. Chroma is exactly zero; neither hue nor alpha varies.",
    "Default endpoints L=.97/.20; linear lightness on either side of the seed using numeric step-label positions.",
    "Illustrative Auto picks nearest reference lightness .97-.77*(step-50)/900, ties to lighter step.",
    "An endpoint seed replaces that endpoint. For an interior seed at/above .97, upper=(1+Ls)/2; at/below .20, lower=Ls/2.",
    "Exact white/black restricted to steps50/950 respectively; interior creation is blocked rather than producing a flat section.",
    "Raw generated coordinates are OKLCH. HEX is an8-bit sRGB preview; duplicate HEX does not imply identical authored coordinates.",
    "No perceptual distinguishability threshold is selected. Only duplicate displayed HEX is flagged.",
    "No gamut mapping needed for neutral examples; chromatic extremes, other step counts and alpha are not qualified.",
    "Endpoint/Auto/placement policy is exploratory, not yet accepted."
  ],
